  "guardrailViolations": [
    "Section 'Session snapshots and encrypted backup' and the Backup API table present encrypted persist_snapshot(&backup_key, generation), load_snapshot, backup_crypto::derive_backup_key and rollback protection as available, with no release caveat. They are implemented only in unreleased pubky-noise rc9 (git HEAD). Published crates.io rc8, and the rc8 that paykit-lib depends on and re-exports, has persist_snapshot(&self), which uploads secret keys unencrypted to /pub. This matches the 'implemented in main but NOT released' category and needs an explicit 'unreleased, git-only' caveat.",
    "Guardrail bullet 'Backup and restore here mean restoring one crate's Noise session' is incomplete: paykit-sdk also offers 'SDK backup/restore' (export/restore of SDK state over an app-owned transport, paykit-sdk/README.md L11-12, L65). Widen the bullet so a reader doesn't take paykit-sdk's backup/restore for Pubky Backup restore (planned) or homeserver mirroring.",
    "'Privacy comes from client-side ciphertext plus unguessable path segments derived from a DH shared secret' overclaims privacy. Unguessable paths exist only when derive_asymmetric_paths + new_with_paths are used; the Quick Start's PubkyNoiseConfig::new(..., \"/pub/data\") writes to a fixed, publicly enumerable /pub path."
  ],
